{
 "system_icons": {
  "note": "The platform theme icon names, so a session can check that an icon exists before writing it into QML. Inventing a theme icon name is the usual way LLM written Sailfish QML fails silently: the Image simply renders nothing. Extracted 2026-10-26 from Jolla's Sailfish Icon Reference page with a script, not from a device.",
  "attribution": "Jolla Mobile Ltd, Sailfish Icon Reference, https://sailfishos.org/develop/docs/jolla-ambient/ . The page states no licence; these are API names, recorded as facts.",
  "how_to_use": "image://theme/<name>, for example image://theme/icon-m-home. Append ?<color> to recolour a monochrome icon, and follow the same colour rules as for text: 'image://theme/icon-s-name' + (listItem.highlighted ? '?' + Theme.highlightColor : '').",
  "size_classes": "icon-s- goes with Theme.iconSizeSmall, icon-m- with iconSizeMedium, icon-l- with iconSizeLarge. icon-splus- is the small plus size used for notification icons, icon-cover- is for cover actions, icon-lock- for the lock screen. Design guidance for each size is in design_guide.json icon_usage.",
  "mime_type_icons": "Theme.iconForMimeType(mimeType) returns one of image://theme/icon-m-file-{apk, audio, formatted, image, note, pdf, other, presentation, rpm, spreadsheet, vcard, video, folder}, falling back to icon-m-file-other.",
  "counts": {
   "small": 66,
   "medium": 415,
   "large": 173,
   "small_plus": 12,
   "cover": 29,
   "lock": 22
  },
  "total": 717,
  "confidence": "vendor_doc, read from the documentation page on 2026-10-26. Presence here is not proof a name exists in a given release. Verification belongs to a session with a device: compare against the theme icon directory on the installed release.",
